  "evaluation": "A ranks first: it correctly treats the disagreement as genuine, identifies the clear population difference, and captures additional differences supported by the fields, including the reported designs. B also gives a sound verdict and primary reason, though it adds an unspecified serum measurement and omits the reported design difference. C reaches the same defensible conclusion but explicitly reclassifies Study A as case-control despite its supplied randomized-trial label. Neither study provides an underpowered-study signal or an effect estimate from Study A that would establish overlapping effects and justify an apparent verdict.",
